# Build hybrids the player can enjoy

- Use self-agency and common sense throughout Apex development and QA. Consider
  how someone would actually create, edit and play a hybrid household. Resolve
  routine choices autonomously within the owner's authorized scope.
- Improve obvious friction with useful, coherent quality-of-life behavior:
  clear selection, relevant icons, compact native-looking controls, explicit
  copy direction, previews, undo and sensible defaults. Avoid duplicate choices
  and complexity that does not help the player.
- Keep exactly one shared Human appearance per Sim. Preserve each occult and
  genuine alternate appearance independently; keep other household Sims isolated.
- Preserve EA's existing form-specific portrait arrangement and behavior,
  especially Alien's. Add missing linking and copying to that arrangement.
- For a form WITHOUT a paired portrait interface, implement an EA-style pair:
  its own occult/special-form portrait above the shared Human below, with full
  Link/Unlink and directional whole/partial Copy support.
- Reuse the portrait interaction pattern without giving another form Vampire
  data, identity, traits or gameplay. Ghost/Human and Imaginary Friend/Human
  remain their own pairs. Selection must target the actual named form, not a
  Vampire substitute or a shared merged appearance.
- Never propagate edits outside the explicitly configured link or copy scope.
  Unlinking stops subsequent propagation; copying affects only its chosen
  destination and included details. Preserve gameplay identity and progression.
- Study the actual code path and exercise the real UI. Correct destructive
  behavior while retaining the permanent preservation guard. Prefer narrowly
  scoped, patch-aware changes; account for other mods using the same resources
  or hooks, and diagnose conflicts without silently overriding their behavior.
- Protect saves, CC and other mods. The owner's original profile remains
  read/copy-only; test in the single disposable profile. Do not trade data
  preservation or compatibility for a shortcut or an unverified feature claim.
- QA visibly distinct edits, every supported category, repeated actual-form
  switches, link/unlink/copy isolation, multi-Sim edits, CAS/Live/MCCC/F11,
  save/cold-load and Tray/Gallery round trips. Unpause where required. Check
  responsiveness and relevant mod compatibility. Fixture passes and duplicate
  record counts do not establish player-visible success or production readiness.
- Follow docs/CAS_SHARED_HUMAN_REQUIREMENTS.md and keep failed/unproved gates open.
